{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "EV-FARE-00115 records fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE with quoted_fare_sgd 34.50, so this trip's distance and time charges were fixed at booking and POL-RD-11 bars any distance-or-time refund however large the excess; the rider's request to be refunded the 'extra distance' must be refused outright, because the detour cost her nothing on those lines.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.fare_model",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The bill reconciles to the cent: the 34.50 quoted fare plus 4.50 of ERP equals the 39.00 charged, so the whole of the excess over the quote is the two ERP lines and not one cent of it is distance or time. Under POL-RD-11(a) the rider's recovery is 39.00 less 34.50 less the 2.50 properly chargeable KPE toll, i.e. 2.00, and the POL-RD-11(b) pass-through correction is not added on top of that figure.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.pol_rd_11_remedy",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The KPE (Defu Flyover towards ECP) charge of 2.50 is properly chargeable under POL-RD-09: that gantry lies on the optimal route and the trace's nearest fix passes 44.5 m from it, far inside the 250 m match radius, so the rider did cross it and none of that 2.50 is refundable.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00115", "EV-FARE-00115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.erp_gantry_proximity.lines[0].nearest_fix.distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The AYE (Alexandra Rd towards Tuas) line is not on the optimal route and the trace's closest approach to that gantry is 5,419 m, more than twenty times the 250 m crossing radius, so it was never crossed; on this record it supports no more than a standalone billing-integrity correction of 2.00 under POL-RD-09(4), which POL-RD-09(1) forbids counting twice and POL-RD-11(b) forbids stacking on any distance refund. That 2.00, not 6.00, is the ceiling on this claim.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00115", "EV-FARE-00115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.erp_gantry_proximity.lines[1].nearest_fix.distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace is unimpaired for policy purposes: 229 fixes at a 10 s interval, 100% coverage, no gaps and a maximum gap of 0 s, so POL-RD-07's gap limbs are not engaged and it is the trace figure of 28.18 km, not the rounded trip_record convenience copy, that POL-RD-01 measures against the 22.4 km optimal.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00115", "EV-TRIP-00115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "payload.max_gap_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Even taken at its highest the deviation is not material: the excess is 5.78 km and 25.80% of the 22.4 km optimal, above the POL-RD-01 establishment gate of 0.8 km and 20% but below the 50% and 8.0 km material gate, so POL-RD-06's uplift to FULL_REFUND and its driver-conduct referral are not engaged and the rider's remedy stays confined to the pass-through lines.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00115", "EV-TRIP-00115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Even if POL-RD-06 were consulted on the profile, the driver records deviation_flags_90d of 1 against completed_trips_90d of 523 — a rate of 0.19%, against thresholds of 3 flags or 5% — so no repeat-deviation pattern is established and no uplift or referral can rest on this driver's record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's account of CTE congestion is tested under POL-RD-13 against the traffic advisory for this trip and nothing else: EV-ADVIS-00115-01 is MISSING with weight 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT — an impairment I disclose — so under POL-RD-08 the assertion carries no weight and supplies no amended optimal. Because no advisory identifier is cited as an exculpatory clause, POL-RD-13(1) applies and this is not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation: the case should be decided on the money, capped at the 2.00 pass-through correction.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00115-01", "EV-GPS-00115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-13", "POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-10"],
      "relies_on": "admissibility.weight_multiplier",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 2.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4) billing integrity — the AYE (Alexandra Rd towards Tuas) gantry line of SGD 2.00 on EV-FARE-00115 was charged although the GPS trace EV-GPS-00115 never came within 5,419 m of that gantry and the gantry is not on the optimal route. Refund it as a standalone pass-through correction and log this phantom charge line for billing-integrity review."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: this trip ran on an upfront quote, and that is what controls the money.\n\nThe deviation is real. EV-GPS-00115 records 28.18 km driven against the 22.40 km platform optimal on EV-TRIP-00115 — an excess of 5.78 km and 25.8%, past both POL-RD-01 gates of 0.8 km and 20%. POL-RD-01 makes the trace figure, not the rounded trip_record copy, the governing one. But EV-FARE-00115 shows fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE with quoted_fare_sgd 34.50, so under POL-RD-11 the distance and time charges were fixed at booking, the detour cost the rider nothing on those lines, and no distance refund is available however large the excess. The request to be refunded the 'extra distance' is refused on that ground; POL-RD-02 does not run.\n\nWhat is refundable is the billing. The rider was quoted 34.50 and charged 39.00. Two ERP lines make up the 4.50 difference. The KPE (Defu Flyover towards ECP) line of 2.50 lies on the optimal route and the trace passes within 44.5 m of it — a crossing, well inside the 250 m match radius — so it is properly chargeable and stands. The AYE (Alexandra Rd towards Tuas) line of 2.00 is phantom: it is not on the optimal route, and the trace's closest approach to it is 5,419 m (at index 0, the first fix of a 100%-coverage trace). Under POL-RD-09(4) that line is refunded in full as a standalone billing-integrity correction. POL-RD-11(a) therefore gives 39.00 charged, less 34.50 quoted, less 2.50 properly chargeable (airport surcharge 0.00, waiting fee 0.00) = 2.00. POL-RD-11(b) is not added on top of (a): the same 2.00 is already excluded from the properly chargeable lines, so counting it again would refund it twice. Amount refunded: 2.00, rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05.\n\nThe driver's account — 'CTE northbound was heavy', repeated in chat MSG-00115-001 at 21:14:10 — is tested under POL-RD-13 against this trip's traffic advisory and nothing else. EV-ADVIS-00115-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, so the POL-RD-03 comparison cannot be run, POL-RD-03 is unavailable, and the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08 and supplies no amended optimal. It changes no money here because the upfront fare fixes the distance line regardless. POL-RD-04 gives the driver nothing either: the rider's only message is 'ok' at 21:14:50 — an acknowledgement of a diversion she was told about, not an instruction, naming no road or place, with waypoint_hint null.\n\nNo escalation. The trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07(a)–(c) (229 fixes, 10 s interval, 100% coverage, max gap 0 s), so no independent-corroboration question arises. No party cited the advisory as an exculpatory clause, so the absent advisory is a gap in the bundle rather than a POL-RD-10(5) contradiction (POL-RD-13(1)). The unmatched AYE line is refunded under POL-RD-09(4), which POL-RD-10(8) expressly carves out. And the deviation is not material (25.8% and 5.78 km, below the 50% and 8.0 km gates), so POL-RD-06 is not engaged; in any event the driver's profile shows deviation_flags_90d of 1 against 523 completed trips in 90 days, far below the 3-flag or 5% pattern thresholds, so it supports no uplift and no conduct referral.\n\nNo driver compensation is due: nothing on this upfront trip was billed by distance, so there is no unbilled-kilometre shortfall.\n\nThis ruling rests on EV-FARE-00115 and EV-GPS-00115, both weight 1.0, so confidence is set at 0.90."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 2.00,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4) billing integrity: the SGD 2.00 AYE (Alexandra Rd towards Tuas) ERP line was charged for a gantry the GPS trace never crossed (closest approach 5,419 m, and the line is not on the optimal route). Refunded in full and recorded as a billing-integrity finding."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.92,
    "explanation": "Both sides are reading the same bill, so I start there. EV-FARE-00115 shows an UPFRONT_QUOTE trip: the fare quoted was SGD 34.50 and SGD 39.00 was charged. The SGD 4.50 difference is not distance or time - it is the two ERP lines, SGD 2.50 on the KPE (Defu Flyover towards ECP) and SGD 2.00 on the AYE (Alexandra Rd towards Tuas). Under POL-RD-11 the distance and time element of an upfront fare is fixed at booking, so the rider's request to refund the 'extra distance' is refused: EV-GPS-00115 (weight 1.0, unimpaired - 229 fixes at a 10 s interval, no gaps, 100% coverage) does measure a real 5.78 km / 25.8% excess over the 22.4 km optimal, past the POL-RD-01 establishment gate, but on an upfront fare that excess costs the rider nothing and buys no refund. The driver is right, and the rider's characterisation of the money is wrong, that the fixed distance and time lines are not the issue; the rider is right, and the driver's statement that 'the fare was fixed anyway, she paid the quote' is wrong, that SGD 4.50 was charged on top of the quote. What remains is the pass-through lines. The KPE line of SGD 2.50 is properly chargeable: the gantry lies on the optimal route and the trace passes within 44.5 m of it, inside the 250 m crossing radius. The AYE line of SGD 2.00 is a phantom: the trace never comes closer than 5,419 m and the line is off the optimal route, so the vehicle was never there. Under POL-RD-09(4) that is a billing-integrity failure and the SGD 2.00 is refunded in full. The refund is therefore 39.00 less 34.50 less 2.50 = SGD 2.00, which is also the figure the ledger itself publishes as pol_rd_11_remedy (2.00). It is not counted twice: POL-RD-11(b) is subsumed in POL-RD-11(a) because the phantom line is already excluded from the properly chargeable total. Driver: your traffic explanation - 'CTE northbound was heavy', repeated in the 21:14:10 chat message - is discarded. POL-RD-13 tests an external-traffic excuse against the traffic advisory for this trip and nothing else, and EV-ADVIS-00115-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT). Because you cited no advisory identifier, POL-RD-13(1) applies: this is a gap in the bundle, not an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, so it is not an escalation and the excuse simply carries no weight. POL-RD-04 does not help you either: the rider's only message was 'ok', an acknowledgement of the diversion you announced, not an instruction, and no waypoint was named. POL-RD-06 is not engaged: the excess is below the 50% and 8.0 km material gates, and your profile (deviation_flags_90d 1 against 523 completed trips in 90 days) shows no pattern, so no uplift and no conduct referral follow. No POL-RD-10 escalation trigger fires: the trace is unimpaired, the trip identifiers match, the timestamps agree, the only unmatched charge line is the one refunded under POL-RD-09(4), and confidence is well above the 0.70 floor. Confidence is 0.92, capped at 1.0 because every fact the ruling rests on is carried by weight-1.0 artifacts (EV-FARE-00115 and EV-GPS-00115), which independently establish the charged total and the AYE non-crossing."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 2.00,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4) billing integrity: EV-FARE-00115 charges SGD 2.00 for the AYE (Alexandra Rd towards Tuas) gantry, which the trace in EV-GPS-00115 never crosses — the closest approach is 5,419.29 m against the 250 m crossing radius, and the line is also flagged on_optimal_route false. The line is refunded in full as a standalone pass-through correction; the matter is recorded for billing-integrity review. POL-RD-10(8) is not engaged, because a line refunded under POL-RD-09(4) is that limb's express carve-out."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "TO THE RIDER: your claim is partly upheld, and SGD 2.00 of the SGD 6.00 you contested comes back to you. This trip ran on an upfront quote. EV-FARE-00115 records quoted_fare_sgd of 34.50 and a total_charged of 39.00, so you paid 4.50 more than the quote shown to you. Of that, 2.50 is the KPE (Defu Flyover towards ECP) gantry: it lies on the optimal route and EV-GPS-00115 shows the vehicle passing within 44.50 m of it, so it is properly chargeable and is not refunded. The other 2.00 is the AYE (Alexandra Rd towards Tuas) gantry, and the trace's closest approach to that gantry is 5,419.29 m — more than twenty times the 250 m crossing radius — so you never crossed it, and that 2.00 is refunded. That is exactly the figure EV-FARE-00115's own derived pol_rd_11_remedy publishes, rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05. Your request to have the extra distance refunded is refused: because the fare model is UPFRONT_QUOTE, POL-RD-11 fixes the distance and time charges at booking and closes the POL-RD-02 route, so no distance refund is available however large the excess. The 5.78 km / 25.8% excess (trace 28.18 km against the 22.40 km optimal) is established under POL-RD-01, but on an upfront fare it produces no money. The deviation is not MATERIAL (25.8% is below the 50% gate and 5.78 km is below the 8.0 km gate), so POL-RD-06 is not engaged, no FULL_REFUND uplift arises, and no driver-conduct referral follows.\n\nTO THE DRIVER: your explanation for leaving the optimal corridor — CTE congestion, repeated in your 21:14:10 message \"CTE very heavy boss, i go KPE then TPE\" — is discarded. POL-RD-13 tests an asserted external traffic cause against the traffic advisory for this trip and nothing else. The bundle holds no such advisory: EV-ADVIS-00115-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, no advisory ID was cited, and so under POL-RD-08 the assertion carries no weight and supplies no amended optimal. Because you cited no advisory identifier, this is not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation — it is a gap in the bundle. The trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07 (229 fixes at 10.0 s, 100% coverage, max_gap_sec 0.0), so POL-RD-10(3) does not apply either; the excess stands at the measured figure and POL-RD-01 runs on the trace figure. POL-RD-04 is unavailable to you: the only rider message is \"ok\", an acknowledgement of a diversion you had already announced, not a request for one, and the admissibility note on EV-CHAT-00115 records the same. POL-RD-13(2) and POL-RD-13(1) both point to a ruling on the money rather than an escalation.\n\nNo escalations fire. POL-RD-10(1) is not met, the confidence here resting on artifacts at weight 1.0; POL-RD-10(6) and (7) do not arise; and POL-RD-10(8) is answered by the POL-RD-09(4) carve-out for the phantom AYE line. The money moved is a partial refund of SGD 2.00 to the rider, and no driver compensation is payable: the upfront fare is not distance-based, there is no unbilled-distance shortfall on the record, and POL-RD-11 places the driver's unrecovered detour cost outside recovery from the rider."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 2.00,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity review: the AYE (Alexandra Rd towards Tuas) ERP line of SGD 2.00 on EV-FARE-00115 was charged for a gantry the trip never crossed — EV-GPS-00115's closest approach to it is 5,419 m and the gantry is not on the optimal route. The line is refunded in full; refer the billing-integrity failure for review of how the line was raised on an upfront-quoted trip."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Both sides agree on the arithmetic, and the record supports it. This was an upfront-quoted trip: EV-FARE-00115 records fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE, quoted_fare_sgd 34.50 and total_charged 39.00, with 0.00 already refunded. Under POL-RD-11 the distance and time charges were fixed at booking, so no distance refund is due however far the car went. EV-GPS-00115 does show a real deviation — 28.18 km driven against the 22.40 km platform optimal, an excess of 5.78 km and 25.8%, past both POL-RD-01 establishment tests (0.8 km / 20%) — but it is below the material gates (50% / 8.0 km), so no POL-RD-06 uplift and no driver-conduct referral arise, and the driver's record (deviation_flags_90d 1 of completed_trips_90d 523) establishes no pattern in any event. The rider's 'ok' at 21:14:50 was an acknowledgement of the driver's announced diversion, not a rider instruction naming a road or place, and waypoint_hint is null, so POL-RD-04 exonerates nothing. The driver's account of CTE congestion, in his statement and in the 21:14:10 chat message, is tested under POL-RD-13 against a traffic advisory for this trip; there is none — EV-ADVIS-00115-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT — so the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08 and supplies no amended route. Because no advisory identifier was cited, this is not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation. The refund sits in the pass-through lines only. Of the 4.50 charged above the quote, 2.50 is the KPE (Defu Flyover towards ECP) gantry, which lies on the optimal route and which the trace passes within 44.5 m, well inside the 250 m radius: it is properly chargeable under POL-RD-09 and is not refunded. The remaining 2.00 is the AYE (Alexandra Rd towards Tuas) gantry, which is not on the optimal route and to which the trace's closest approach is 5,419 m — a billing-integrity failure under POL-RD-09(4), refunded in full as a standalone correction. Refund = 39.00 charged_total less 34.50 quoted_fare less 2.50 properly chargeable KPE ERP = 2.00, rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05. Nothing is added on top of that figure (POL-RD-09(1), POL-RD-11(b)), and no driver compensation is due, the fare being an upfront quote with no billed distance shortfall. The profile fields used are only the counters the clauses name (POL-GEN-01). The deciding facts are carried by EV-GPS-00115 and EV-FARE-00115, both at weight 1.0, so confidence is not discounted; no escalation trigger under POL-RD-10 fires, the AYE line being its express POL-RD-09(4) carve-out."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
